Z||000000||Brian84SE||05-04-2000||12:28 PM||||I've read your article on actuators for climate control. My vent actuator is not working. Is this the "God help you if your top one doesn't work" one?  Do I need to pull the dash or will removing the right speaker do it?  Any more details you had would be helpfull.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||05-04-2000||02:28 PM||||Welllllll Actually I've had a dash out. The one motor as you know is behind the radio. The cable from the hot/cold slider goes to the top of the system below the speaker.<P>The bad news.<P>I still don't know where that other motor is. It's not on the top or front that I saw it. I'll be having a trip to the scrap yard tomorow. I'll have a better look. It was raining when I was there last. I'll also be pulling my dash soon to replace it. I'll check then if I can't get to the yard. I have a real bad feeling is on the front side of the MVAC system. Like I said, I'll look tomorow. I want a spare one of those.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-05-2000||02:06 PM||||I looked in the yard today. I think I found it. I think. It looks to be on the bottom of the system. I think you can get it off from the pasenger's side, maybe.  I can hardly see in there even with plenty of light and this is even with the cars whole dash out. <P>It's really nasty to get to. It looks like it faces the pasenger side and is between the duct work and the tank hump.<P>You'll likely need a long flexy shaft screw driver. Even after you got the 2 screws out I don't know if you'll have enough room to get the clip off and back on. I beleive there is only one linkage on that one. so that should help.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brian84SE||05-05-2000||09:42 PM||||Thanks, I'll take a look this weekend at it||||reg||1
